## Pinned upstream sources for the vendored drop-in files under lib/. SHCL
## ships as one self-contained file per language, so it is copied in rather than
## required as a module: that keeps this program at standard library plus its own
## source, and keeps the go directive off upstream's (higher) floor. The cost of
## copying is that drift is invisible, which is what the pin plus
## utility/check-vendor.bash buys back.
##
## One line per vendored file:  LOCAL_PATH|OWNER/REPO|TAG|PATH_IN_UPSTREAM
## LOCAL_PATH is relative to the repo root. TAG is the upstream release the copy
## was taken from; bump it in the same commit that refreshes the file.
VENDOR_PINS=(
	"lib/shcl/shcl.go|jim-collier/shcl|v1.2.0|source/go/shcl.go"
)
